{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And for the man he did not find a helper.</b> And why did He not create her at first? Rather, the Holy One, blessed be He, foresaw that he was destined to bring a charge against her, and did not create her for him at first until he demanded her explicitly with his mouth, and immediately — 'and a deep sleep fell.'" "<b>As his counterpart.</b> From one resembling him in image, likeness, and form, as the Jerusalem Targum renders: 'a fitting partner for him.' And therefore it writes <b>he did not find a helper as his counterpart</b>, even though he might have found for himself many attendants and servants."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:30.953680496Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}